{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs PyPy 3 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following PyPy 3 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nThis version of the problem differs from the next one only in the constraint on $$$n$$$.Note that the memory limit in this problem is lower than in others.You have a vertical strip with $$$n$$$ cells, numbered consecutively from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ from top to bottom.You also have a token that is initially placed in cell $$$n$$$. You will move the token up until it arrives at cell $$$1$$$.Let the token be in cell $$$x &gt; 1$$$ at some moment. One shift of the token can have either of the following kinds:   Subtraction: you choose an integer $$$y$$$ between $$$1$$$ and $$$x-1$$$, inclusive, and move the token from cell $$$x$$$ to cell $$$x - y$$$.  Floored division: you choose an integer $$$z$$$ between $$$2$$$ and $$$x$$$, inclusive, and move the token from cell $$$x$$$ to cell $$$\\lfloor \\frac{x}{z} \\rfloor$$$ ($$$x$$$ divided by $$$z$$$ rounded down). Find the number of ways to move the token from cell $$$n$$$ to cell $$$1$$$ using one or more shifts, and print it modulo $$$m$$$. Note that if there are several ways to move the token from one cell to another in one shift, all these ways are considered distinct (check example explanation for a better understanding).\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the PyPy 3 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef add(x, y):\n    return ((x % mod) + (y % mod)) % mod\n\ndef solve():\n    dp = [0] * (n + 1)\n    prefix = [0] * (n + 2)\n    \n    dp[n] = 1\n    \n    for i in range(n, 0, -1):\n        prefix[i] = prefix[i + 1]\n        dp[i] = (dp[i] + prefix[i]) % mod\n        \n        for k in range(2 * i, n + 1):\n            if k // 2 < i:\n                break\n                \n            for j in range(2, k + 1):\n                if k // j == i:\n                    dp[i] = (dp[i] + dp[k]) % mod\n                if k // j < i:\n                    break\n        \n        prefix[i] = (prefix[i] + dp[i]) % mod\n    \n    return dp[1]\n\ndata = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\nidx = 0\nwhile idx < len(data):\n    n = int(data[idx]); mod = int(data[idx+1]); idx += 2\n    print(solve())\n    break\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    dp = [0] * (n + 1)\n    dp[n] = 1\n    \n    # prefix sum array to optimize the subtraction moves\n    prefix = [0] * (n + 2)\n    \n    for i in range(n, 0, -1):\n        # Add all ways from positions > i via subtraction moves\n        # For subtraction: from position j > i, we can move to i by subtracting (j-i)\n        # So we need to add dp[j] for all j > i\n        # Using prefix sum: prefix[i+1] = sum of dp[i+1] to dp[n]\n        dp[i] = (dp[i] + prefix[i + 1]) % mod\n        \n        # For division moves: from position j, we can move to floor(j/z) = i\n        # This means j is in range [i*z, i*z + z - 1] for z >= 2\n        # So for each z >= 2, j ranges from i*z to min(n, i*z + z - 1)\n        z = 2\n        while True:\n            start = i * z\n            if start > n:\n                break\n            end = min(n, i * z + z - 1)\n            # Add dp[j] for j in [start, end]\n            # Using prefix sum: prefix[start] - prefix[end+1]\n            dp[i] = (dp[i] + (prefix[start] - prefix[end + 1])) % mod\n            z += 1\n        \n        # Update prefix sum: prefix[i] = dp[i] + prefix[i+1]\n        prefix[i] = (prefix[i + 1] + dp[i]) % mod\n    \n    return dp[1] % mod\n\ndata = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\nif data:\n    idx = 0\n    while idx < len(data):\n        n = int(data[idx]); mod = int(data[idx+1]); idx += 2\n        print(solve())\n        break\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.446407547220588e-05, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0010425376240164042, -7.867782187531702e-06, -0.0005548844928853214, -0.003946731332689524, -0.04386933147907257, -0.18080440163612366, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.0367397665977478, -4.768370445162873e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -8.821448318485636e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -0.00013982271775603294, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.007608364336192608, -0.7805320024490356, -0.011052576825022697, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.08193110674619675, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.34988898038864136, -0.6569579243659973, -0.31172439455986023, -0.009956695139408112, -0.5832201838493347, -0.11610103398561478, -0.4695231318473816, -0.16704405844211578, -0.020645134150981903, -0.07019919157028198, -8.34461570775602e-06, -0.20389991998672485, -0.029858142137527466, -5.006777428206988e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.576272320060525e-06, 0.0, -8.344646857949556e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -0.009755908511579037, -0.00011419598013162613, -0.02630288526415825, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.22594761848449707, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.018377041444182396, -1.19209282445